      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-06T15:38:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure if we want to make this available to apps. This might be too powerful to be provided to apps. WDYT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 426,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 431,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "2704543c167c5d1e5e266207d9d7b6373e478bfa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e3ec908c_9bc225db",
        "filename": "javalib/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachineConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 431,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-06T16:27:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well. We are now using this in some of our benchmark tests, and it would be nice if we built those against the system API. And if we want to disallow priv apps from using this we\u0027d need to put this behind the custom VM permission, but we can then grant that to the test app.\n\nIf crosvm were running in the app\u0027s cgroup, then the set of CPUs available to it would be controlled by Android. (E.g. I think a background app only gets at most one CPU.)\n\nBut it isn\u0027t so you\u0027re probably right.",
      "parentUuid": "a139cfb4_02904f53",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 426,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 431,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "2704543c167c5d1e5e266207d9d7b6373e478bfa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "778b8792_986a71bf",
        "filename": "javalib/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachineConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 431,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-06T16:45:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For ordinary apps, we definitely want that this is uncontrollable (i.e. inherited from its parent). For platform\u0027s internal use (e.g. compos), we want to have control, but they don\u0027t need to use this Java API. So, I don\u0027t think this API is quite useful modulo tests. What about dropping @SystemApi here and also enforcing that overriding cpu affinity needs a privileged permission? (the latter could be done as a separate change) Tests could be built with private APIs.",
      "parentUuid": "e3ec908c_9bc225db",
